# Server settings live in server.config.
#
# Leave VITE_API_BASE unset for development, same-origin deployments, and
# packaged iOS, Android, and macOS builds. Vite proxies development requests,
# and installed apps let the reader choose a server at runtime. A baked-in
# loopback address points at the reader's own device.
#
# Vite reads environment files from apps/web, the web app project. It does
# not load a .env at the repository root, including a copy of this file.
#
# For a browser frontend intentionally hosted at a different address, pass
# the variable only for that production build:
#
#   VITE_API_BASE=https://books.example.com npm run build -w @operalibre/web
#
# Also add that frontend's origin to allowed_origins. See docs/configuration.md.
